          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. How We Chose</h2>
<p>
            We have not used or tested these machines. They were chosen from the makers' own stores
            and specifications, an authorised retailer's listing, launch and pricing coverage from
            VR trade press, and hands-on impressions from independent reviewers, and the claims on
            this page stay within what those sources support.
          </p>
          <p>
            The field is small, so the main job was establishing what is actually for sale to a
            home buyer in the US today. Several names that come up in VR treadmill searches are not:
            Infinadeck's motorised omnidirectional treadmill is sold to enterprise, medical and
            government customers, with no published price, and its maker has talked about a consumer
            version without announcing one. KAT VR's Walk Mini S and Virtuix's Omni One Enterprise
            are business products. We list only what a person can order for home use now.
          </p>
          <p>
            For each configuration we checked the price on the maker's store, what is in the box,
            the headsets it supports, the user height and weight limits, and the footprint, and we
            looked for at least one independent source for each. Where an independent source gave a
            different figure, we said so rather than choosing. We searched cpsc.gov for both makers
            and found no recall or warning.
          </p>
